// What the payment ledger says per application. The ledger is a reference source: these
// rules only add up what it recorded. No rule of the scheme reads them; calc/drift.yaml compares the
// total with the award. Only accepted payments count (the seal: ledger_payment__accepted); a payment a
// close refuses is in ledger_payment__refused.

// An accepted payment with its application and its amount.
.decl ledger_line(application: symbol, payment: symbol, cents: number)
ledger_line(a, p, c) :- ledger_payment__accepted(p), ledger_payment__application(p, a), ledger_payment__amount(p, c).

// An application the ledger has paid something for.
.decl paid(application: symbol)
paid(a) :- ledger_line(a, _, _).

// What the ledger paid for an application, over all its payments.
.decl ledger_paid(application: symbol, cents: number)
ledger_paid(a, t) :- paid(a), t = sum c : { ledger_line(a, _, c) }.

.output ledger_paid
